$-- No-op override. Quarto's default fonts.latex loads `unicode-math`
$-- under LuaLaTeX/XeLaTeX, which breaks macros sharing a name with a math
$-- operator (e.g. \mp) and breaks \euro right after math mode. This
$-- extension loads classic Type 1 fonts itself (include-in-header.tex),
$-- so unicode-math is never needed.
